WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.927
You will,

00:00:00.927 --> 00:00:02.928
I guarantee it,

00:00:02.928 --> 00:00:07.185
at some point,&nbsp;become 
embroiled in a complicated,

00:00:07.185 --> 00:00:11.102
confusing, ugly, gut-wrenching moral dilemma. 

00:00:11.102 --> 00:00:13.424
So how do you prepare for that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.568
By reading theories of ethics and 
understanding&nbsp;what they say,

00:00:18.568 --> 00:00:20.000
what they mean,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.973
how they purport to help us 
make better decisions

00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:24.488
and become better people.

00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:25.936
Just reading these theories

00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:29.589
is no guarantee that you will 
actually make&nbsp;the right choice.

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:32.103
But if you've prepared,

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:34.904
you will increase your odds of success.

00:00:34.904 --> 00:00:37.046
Understanding&nbsp;ethical theories

00:00:37.046 --> 00:00:40.335
is how we increase our chances of success

00:00:40.335 --> 00:00:42.650
at simply being human beings

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.979
who&nbsp;have to negotiate with other human beings.

